    "subtype": "success",
    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the `frai gate init --ci` bug. The issue was in how the `frai` CLI was passing arguments to the `frai-gate` subcommand.\n\n### The Problem\nThe `gate` command in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` was using Commander's option parsing with `.allowUnknownOption(true)`, but with positional arguments like `[args...]`, the flags like `--ci` were not being properly captured and passed through to `frai-gate`.\n\n### The Solution\nInstead of relying on Commander's option parsing (which doesn't work well with the `[args...]` format), I modified the action handler to directly extract all arguments after `\"gate\"` from `process.argv` and pass them directly to `frai-gate`:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : [];\nconst { spawnSync } = await import('child_process');\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...gateArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\nThis ensures that **all** flags and arguments (`--ci`, `--out`, `--smart`, `--json`, `--print`, etc.) are properly passed through to `frai-gate`.\n\n### Verification\n\u2705 `frai gate init --ci` - Creates both FRAI-SPEC.md and .github/workflows/rai-gate.yml  \n\u2705 `frai gate init` - Creates only FRAI-SPEC.md (no workflow)  \n\u2705 `frai gate init --out custom.md --ci` - Creates custom.md and the workflow  \n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and is ready to use.",
